# Intent: A cartoon face style as data (docs/design/face-styles.md, owner request 2026-11-19): a glossy eye design, three color slots and a tongue. The eye is a white oval, a colored iris that follows the gaze and rests looking up and to the side, a dark pupil and one small highlight. A recipe carries the iris color, the eye-white color and the tongue color in its two spare bytes (byte 14 the iris, byte 15 the tongue in the high four bits and the white in the low four; each is an index into one 15-color table, 0 meaning the style's default), so the recipe stays 44 bytes and older recipes (both bytes zero) read as before. The shape list gains three color slots; the avatar fills them when the style or the face color changes. An open smile (a thick mouth stroke) draws a small tongue in its lower middle. The iris is the face color unless that is white, then brown; the eye white is near-white; the tongue is pink. Original shapes only.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_look_core.h and firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/default/ (ours, patches X01, V10, UXF01)
# Check after a flash: install the cartoon style asset and apply it; the eyes are white with a colored iris looking up and aside, the smile shows a pink tongue when it opens, a happy eye closes to an arch, a sleepy lid covers the top; a recipe with both color bytes zero draws the default colors; the memory row is the same as for any other recipe.
# Kconfig: none
# Memory cost: three colors (6 bytes of internal RAM), no objects. Flash about 0.4 KB.

